            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for demand (for goods), then the Bengali for to fluctuate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: মেঘ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মেঘ — megh — \"a cloud\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আকাশে কালো মেঘ দেখে আমরা ছাতা নিলাম। ākāshe kālo megh dekhe āmrā chhātā nilām. Seeing dark clouds in the sky, we took umbrellas."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Thunder is said to be the clouds calling: মেঘ (megh) ডাকে."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মেঘ (megh) is Sanskrit megha, \"a cloud\" (Monier-Williams), a word Monier-Williams links with mih, to sprinkle: the cloud is the sprinkler."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
